<title>USA: U.S. March consumer prices rose 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. March consumer prices rose 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department monthly Consumer Price Index (CPI-U), 1982-84 equals 100:</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  Seasonally Adj.    Unadjusted</p>
<p>    -			   Mar    Feb     Mar97/96</p>
<p> All Items		    0.1    0.3	2.8</p>
<p> -Excluding Food/Energy   0.2    0.2	2.5</p>
<p> Energy			-1.7    0.3	4.8</p>
<p> Food and Beverages	Unch    0.3	3.3</p>
<p> Food			  Unch    0.3	3.3</p>
<p> CPI-Urban Consumers-X  160.0  159.6	N/A</p>
<p>X-Data unadjusted. N/A-Not Available.  </p>
